   "about": "I'm a software engineer and three-time startup founder (SpecFrog, 🤫) with a successful exit currently working on a stealth startup. I studied Computer Science at FIT, realized I didn't need to pay $50k/yr to read my textbooks, so I dropped out to work at a startup.\n\nI have over 14 years of experience developing web applications and have worked on various projects and platforms including AI/ML, construction sales, health care, social media, marketing automation, and data analytics.\n\nI have contributed to the development of innovative solutions, at AWS, Bank of America, Sherwin Williams, Red Hat, Dataminr, USPM, Availity, and multiple other small businesses as well as founding several startups. \n\nI am passionate about learning new technologies and best practices, and collaborating with other talented engineers and stakeholders. I'm a huge fan of Functional Programming. I am always looking for opportunities to apply my skills and knowledge to create impactful and user-friendly web experiences that solve real-world problems and meet customer needs.",
